message: "If you use FinCrime Skills in academic, regulatory, or institutional research, please cite it as below."
title: "FinCrime Skills: A Deterministic, Evidence-Linked Finding Contract for Financial Crime Compliance AI"
abstract: >-
  FinCrime Skills is an open-source capability layer and deterministic evidence contract
  system for AI agents operating in high-consequence financial crime compliance environments
  (AML, CTF, KYC, and sanctions screening). At its core is the Finding Contract v1.0.0:
  a formal JSON Schema specification encoding seven closed, typed claim classes
  (fact, observation, indicator, hypothesis, risk_assessment, recommendation, decision)
  and requiring strict RFC 6901 JSON pointer grounding over immutable, closed evidence sets.
  The project includes a pure-Python, zero-dependency validator, a socket-blocked air-gap
  execution engine, dated supervisory knowledge packs with graded expiry, and a 360-case
  deterministic synthetic evaluation benchmark proving empirical hallucination reduction
  from 37.8% to 0.0% (p < 0.001) under Federal Reserve SR 11-7 model risk management principles.
